Figure 2. (a) SEM image of the as-synthesized COP-TPP@MOF. (b) and (c) TEM and HRTEM images of COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900. Lattice fringe at 0.206 and \(0.340\ \mathrm{nm}\) refers to \(\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{N}\) (111) and C (002), respectively. (d) SEM image of the as-synthesized COP-TPP. (e) and (f) TEM and HRTEM images of the COP-TPP(Fe)-900. Lattice fringe at 0.290 and \(0.340\ \mathrm{nm}\) refers to \(\mathrm{Fe}_{3}\mathrm{N}\) (101) and C (002), respectively.
Figure 3. ORR electrocatalytic performances of catalysts. (a) CV curves of MOF-900, COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900 and COP-TPP(Fe)-900 at a scan rate of \(100\ \mathrm{mv\ s^{-1}}\). (b) LSV curves and (c) corresponding Tafel plots of Pt/C, MOF-900, COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900 and COP-TPP(Fe)-900 at a scan rate of \(5\ \mathrm{mv\ s^{-1}}\) with \(1600\ \mathrm{rpm}\). (d) The electron transfer number per oxygen molecule on various catalysts at \(0.6\ \mathrm{V}\) vs. RHE. ① for MOF-900, ② for COP-TPP(Fe)-900, ③ for COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900, ④ for Pt/C. (e) LSV curves of COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900 before and after 5000 cycles, respectively. Inset shows the corresponding Tafel plots of COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900 before and after 5,000 potential cycles. (f) The capacitive current at \(1.1\ \mathrm{V}\) vs. RHE at various scan rates for COP-TPP(Fe)@MOF-900 and COP-TPP(Fe)-900, respectively.
